{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הניחה", :translit "haneichah", :gloss "leave Me / let Me"} {:he "הניחה לי", :translit "haneichah li", :gloss "leave Me"} {:he "הניחה אותי", :translit "haneichah oti", :gloss "leave Me"} {:he "משני את העמודים", :translit "mishneh et ha-amudim", :gloss "he changed the columns"} {:he "שמשון", :translit "shimshon", :gloss "Samson"} {:he "שהרג בהם במותו יותר ממה שהמית בחייו", :translit "she-harag bahem be-moto yoter mi-mah she-heimit be-chayav", :gloss "that he killed among them in his death more than he put to death in his lifetime"} {:he "ויחר אפי בהם ואכלם", :translit "veyichar api bahem ve'ochlam", :gloss "and My anger will burn against them and I will consume them"} {:he "שכילם", :translit "shechilam", :gloss "that he consumed them"} {:he "והמית בהם כל שריהם", :translit "veheimit bahem kol sareihem", :gloss "and put to death among them all their officers"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["הניחה לי" "הניחה אותי"]} {:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "הניחה לי ויחר אפי בהם ואכלם", :spells "משני את העמודים"} {:kind :other, :note "Phrases about destruction by fire/death are equated between God's threat against Israel and Samson's vengeance."}], :frame {:text "In Judges 16:30, Samson says 'let me die with the Philistines' and the verse states that those he killed at his death were more than those he had killed in his lifetime. The phrase 'ויחר אפי בהם ואכלם' (Exodus 32:10) also occurs in the aftermath of the Golden Calf narrative (Exodus 32:10–11). The idiom 'הניחה לי' appears twice in the Masorah, here in Exodus 32:10 and in Judges 16:28 where Samson says 'הניחה אותי' to God.", :sources ["Judges 16:30" "Judges 16:28" "Exodus 32:10" "Exodus 32:11"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ואכלם", :translit "ve'ochlam", :gloss "and I will consume them"} {:he "ואכלם ואמחצם", :translit "ve'ochlam ve'achatzem", :gloss "and I will consume them and crush them"} {:he "דין", :translit "din", :gloss "this one / here"} {:he "שאין פרוענות שאין בה פרעון ממעשה העגל", :translit "she'ein pera'onut she'ein bah pera'on ma'aseh ha'egel", :gloss "there is no punishment that does not contain retribution from the incident of the calf"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ואכלם" "ואכלם ואמחצם"]} {:kind :other, :note "Midrashic principle: every punishment Israel suffers contains retribution for the Golden Calf."}], :frame {:text "The two Masorah occurrences of 'ואכלם' are at Exodus 32:10 and Deuteronomy 32:42, where the verse reads 'ואכלם ואמחצם' — 'and I will consume them and crush them.' The principle that every punishment Israel receives contains retribution for the Golden Calf is expressed in the Talmud: Rabbi Yitzchak said, 'there is no punishment that comes to the world that does not contain one twenty-fourth of the first calf' (Sanhedrin 102a).", :sources ["Sanhedrin 102a" "Exodus 32:10" "Deuteronomy 32:42"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ואעשה אותך", :translit "ve'e'eseh otcha", :gloss "and I will make you"} {:he "מלא וי\"ו", :translit "malei vav", :gloss "plene with vav"} {:he "שיצאו ממך ו' מאות אלף", :translit "sheyatzu mimcha shesh me'ot elef", :gloss "that from you will come forth six hundred thousand"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The vav of malei spelling signals 600,000 descendants."}], :frame {:text "God tells Moses, 'ואעשה אותך לגוי גדול' — 'and I will make you into a great nation' (Exodus 32:10). The word 'ואעשה' is written plene with a vav after the shin. Israel is counted as approximately six hundred thousand men at the Exodus (Exodus 12:37, Numbers 1:46).", :sources ["Exodus 32:10" "Exodus 12:37" "Numbers 1:46"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["הניחה לי" "הניחה אותי"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "הניחה לי", :refs ["Exodus 32:10"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "הניחה אותי", :refs ["Judges 16:26"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "הניחה לי ויחר אפי בהם ואכלם", :spells "משני את העמודים", :letters ["ה" "י" "ר" "י" "ם" "ם"], :